-- תחום תנאי שירות עובדי הוראה — תקנון שירות עובדי הוראה (the introduction)
-- The department's page introducing the takanon. Its rule is one of
-- precedence: the takanon is being updated, so where it does not match a
-- collective agreement, the law, a director-general's circular, a ministry
-- procedure or a more recent circular to the owners, those prevail. It also
-- says that the binding text is that of the sources the takanon cites, that
-- its amounts are not kept up to date, and how "% of the combined salary"
-- is read. The rest describes the takanon.

IMPORT prelude

§ `תקנון שירות עובדי הוראה — מבוא`

-- akn:hc_1 The portal's breadcrumb and the page title; no rule.

§§ `Precedence over the takanon`

DECLARE `kind of source` IS ONE OF
    `a collective agreement`
    `a provision of law`
    `a director-general's circular`
    `a Ministry of Education procedure`
    `a circular to the owning bodies`
    `another source`

@desc A source whose words do not match the takanon on a point.
DECLARE `conflicting source` HAS
    `source kind`   IS A `kind of source`
    `source issued` IS A DATE @desc the date the source was issued or signed

-- hc_2 ¶1–2: "the takanon is being updated; therefore wherever the takanon
-- does not match collective agreements, the provisions of the law,
-- director-general's circulars, procedures of the Ministry of Education or
-- more recent circulars to the owning bodies, what they say prevails".
-- F-terms-a: "עדכניים יותר" is read with the nearest noun, the circulars to
-- the owning bodies; the other four prevail whatever their date.
-- F-terms-b: "more recent" than the takanon, whose sections carry dates of
-- their own amendments and the whole none: the date the provision at issue
-- was last amended is an input.
@ref akn:hc_2 akn:hc_2/p2
GIVEN s IS A `conflicting source`
      `date the takanon's provision was last amended` IS A DATE @desc the amendment date the provision's own section prints ("סעיף זה תוקן ב…"); the text names no date of the takanon as a whole
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `prevails over the takanon` s `date the takanon's provision was last amended` IF
    CONSIDER s's `source kind`
    WHEN `a circular to the owning bodies` THEN
        s's `source issued` `is after` `date the takanon's provision was last amended`
    WHEN `another source` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

DECLARE `governing text` IS ONE OF
    `the takanon's own words`
    `the words of the prevailing sources` HAS `prevailing sources` IS A LIST OF `conflicting source`

@export default Which text governs a point on which the takanon and other sources do not match, under the department's introduction to the takanon
GIVEN sources IS A LIST OF `conflicting source` @desc the sources whose words do not match the takanon on the point
      `date the takanon's provision was last amended` IS A DATE @desc the amendment date of the takanon provision at issue
GIVETH A `governing text`
DECIDE `the text that governs` sources `date the takanon's provision was last amended` IS
    LET prevailing MEANS filter (GIVEN s YIELD `prevails over the takanon` s `date the takanon's provision was last amended`) sources
    IN IF null prevailing
       THEN `the takanon's own words`
       ELSE `the words of the prevailing sources` prevailing

GIVEN d IS A DATE, e IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE d `is after` e IF
    DATE_SERIAL d GREATER THAN DATE_SERIAL e

-- akn:hc_3 The heading "with the publication of the takanon"; the paragraphs follow.
-- akn:hc_3/p1 Who prepared the takanon and what it covers; a description, no rule.
-- akn:hc_3/p2 akn:hc_3/p3 akn:hc_3/p4 akn:hc_3/p5 What the takanon contains and whom it may help, as questions and answers; a description, no rule.
-- akn:hc_3/p6 The heading "the takanon's legal force"; the paragraph follows.

§§ `The takanon's legal force`

DECLARE `wording of a provision` IS ONE OF
    `the takanon's wording`
    `the wording of the sources the takanon cites`

-- hc_3 ¶7: "the binding wording, application and scope of the takanon's
-- provisions are those of the sources it cites"; its amounts are not
-- updated, "because of the frequency of the changes"; for current amounts,
-- one applies to the office.
@ref akn:hc_3/p7
`the binding wording of a takanon provision` MEANS `the wording of the sources the takanon cites`

@ref akn:hc_3/p7
`an amount printed in the takanon is kept current` MEANS FALSE

DECLARE `amount action` IS ONE OF
    `apply to the office for the current amounts`

@ref akn:hc_3/p7
GIVETH A DEONTIC `reader of the takanon` `amount action`
DECIDE `asking the office for the amounts` IS
    PARTY `a reader`
    MAY   `apply to the office for the current amounts`

DECLARE `reader of the takanon` IS ONE OF
    `a reader`

-- hc_3 ¶8: "% of the combined salary" means every component that forms the
-- base of the allowances, unless the text says in terms that the combined
-- salary alone is meant. (This is how section 1.11's L4 reads the split
-- allowance's "5% מהשכר המשולב", F-1.11-d.)
DECLARE `percentage wording` IS ONE OF
    `a percentage of the combined salary`
    `a percentage of the combined salary alone, said in terms`

DECLARE `base meant` IS ONE OF
    `every component that forms the base of the allowances`
    `the combined salary alone`

@ref akn:hc_3/p8
GIVEN w IS A `percentage wording`
GIVETH A `base meant`
DECIDE `the base a percentage is taken of` w IS
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `a percentage of the combined salary` THEN `every component that forms the base of the allowances`
    WHEN `a percentage of the combined salary alone, said in terms` THEN `the combined salary alone`

-- akn:hc_3/p9 The signature: the officer in charge of teaching employees' conditions of service; no rule.

§§ `Worked examples`

-- The dates are placeholders; 12.1.2004 is the amendment date section 1.11
-- prints, 19.11.2002 the review date section 1.9.1 prints.
`a 1989 collective agreement` MEANS `conflicting source` `a collective agreement` (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 5 1989)
`a 2003 circular to the owners` MEANS `conflicting source` `a circular to the owning bodies` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2003)
`a 2010 circular to the owners` MEANS `conflicting source` `a circular to the owning bodies` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2010)

#ASSERT `prevails over the takanon` `a 1989 collective agreement` (DATE_FROM_DMY 12 1 2004)
#ASSERT `prevails over the takanon` `a 2010 circular to the owners` (DATE_FROM_DMY 12 1 2004)
#ASSERT NOT `prevails over the takanon` `a 2003 circular to the owners` (DATE_FROM_DMY 12 1 2004)
#ASSERT `the text that governs` EMPTY (DATE_FROM_DMY 12 1 2004) EQUALS `the takanon's own words`
#ASSERT `the base a percentage is taken of` `a percentage of the combined salary` EQUALS `every component that forms the base of the allowances`

-- F-terms-a's evidence: an agreement older than the provision it conflicts
-- with prevails if "more recent" qualifies the circulars alone, and does not
-- if it qualifies every source in the list.
GIVEN s IS A `conflicting source`, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `prevails if every source must be more recent` s d IF
    (NOT (s's `source kind` EQUALS `another source`)) AND (s's `source issued` `is after` d)

`the two readings of "more recent" part on an older agreement` MEANS
        `prevails over the takanon` `a 1989 collective agreement` (DATE_FROM_DMY 12 1 2004)
    AND (NOT `prevails if every source must be more recent` `a 1989 collective agreement` (DATE_FROM_DMY 12 1 2004))
#ASSERT `the two readings of "more recent" part on an older agreement`

-- F-terms-b's evidence: a circular of June 2003 is more recent than section
-- 1.9.1 (reviewed 19.11.2002) and older than section 1.11 (amended
-- 12.1.2004): "the takanon" has no one date to be more recent than.
`a circular of June 2003 is newer than one section and older than another` MEANS
        `prevails over the takanon` `a 2003 circular to the owners` (DATE_FROM_DMY 19 11 2002)
    AND (NOT `prevails over the takanon` `a 2003 circular to the owners` (DATE_FROM_DMY 12 1 2004))
#ASSERT `a circular of June 2003 is newer than one section and older than another`

-- F-terms-c's evidence: an agreement and a newer circular both depart from
-- the takanon on one point; both prevail over it, and the rule does not say
-- which of the two governs.
`two prevailing sources` MEANS
    `the text that governs` (LIST `a 1989 collective agreement`, `a 2010 circular to the owners`) (DATE_FROM_DMY 12 1 2004)

GIVEN g IS A `governing text`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `sources that govern` g IS
    CONSIDER g
    WHEN `the takanon's own words` THEN 1
    WHEN `the words of the prevailing sources` ps THEN count ps

`the rule leaves two sources governing one point` MEANS
    `sources that govern` `two prevailing sources` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the rule leaves two sources governing one point`
